<h1>Star Science Fiction</h1>

Two magazines were supposed to have been called <i>Star</i> in the early 50's: 
one was to be edited by William Tenn for Gnome in 1950, the other one
eventually saw the light of day as <i>Cosmos</i> in 1953. The magazine
cataloged here was edited by Frederik Pohl for Ballantine in 1958 and was
supposed to be a continuation of their successful line of eponymous
paperback anthologies (only three had been printed by 1958.) The first
issue of the projected quarterly was much delayed and its sales were
disappointing, so by the end of 1958 Ballantine decided to go back to the
anthology format, which lasted for another three issues.
